think Continued the loop from the selection_summary lap. That lap named the next crux-first siblings: an object-count-in-region summary, a per-selection bounding-box union, a descriptor join over a selection, or a codec read. Took the per-selection bounding-box union -- the group frame -- as the extent companion to the summary's facts, a distinct durable surface primitive that closes cleanly with a GREEN witness and no gate.
think Standfast first: every living REDS row is CLOSED or Released, only #75 rests as custody-gated errata. Line clear.
think Designed the decisive crux to mirror box-is-a-prefilter one level up, at the selection: a union box CONTAINS more than it SELECTS. Placed three blocks at corner, middle, far corner; selecting the two corners (skipping the middle) frames a box that wholly holds the UNSELECTED middle block, so box_contains_object is TRUE for an object the selection never named -- containment of a box is not membership of the set. The union also exceeds either member on both axes and its area covers the background between them.
obs Built image/selection_bounds.rye (selection_bbox unions the selected boxes with a running min/max; Box with width/height/area; box_contains_object; validate_selection refuses BadSelection at the edge, empty refuses EmptySelection) + tools/selection_bounds_witness.rish (native contains, REDS #85).
